WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.652 --> 00:00:01.519
podcast, margin of error.

00:00:01.653 --> 00:00:03.888
You can find it on our favorite

00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:07.258
podcast app or at cnn.com/audio.

00:00:07.392 --> 00:00:08.393
&gt;&gt;&gt; Donald Trump is finally

00:00:08.493 --> 00:00:10.061
hitting the 2024 campaign trial,

00:00:10.395 --> 00:00:12.030
starting with what he called a,

00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:14.399
quote, intimate event in south

00:00:14.399 --> 00:00:14.766
Carolina.

00:00:14.766 --> 00:00:16.735
But the Daily Show's Jordan

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:17.769
Klepper spoke to some of the

00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:19.170
people waiting to get in,

00:00:19.304 --> 00:00:20.572
including these two women, who

00:00:20.705 --> 00:00:21.706
insist trump is still in charge

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:22.407
of the U.S. Military.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:23.208
Yes, I said that.

00:00:23.341 --> 00:00:24.843
You heard that correctly.

00:00:24.976 --> 00:00:26.711
That trump is still in charge of

00:00:26.845 --> 00:00:27.846
the U.S. Military, or at least

00:00:27.979 --> 00:00:28.479
one of them anyway.

00:00:28.513 --> 00:00:31.683
Take a listen.

00:00:31.816 --> 00:00:33.718
&gt;&gt; The military were put in

00:00:33.852 --> 00:00:34.419
charge in 2018 when president

00:00:34.552 --> 00:00:36.421
trump signed an executive order.

00:00:36.488 --> 00:00:37.422
&gt;&gt; The American military arms

00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:39.023
that are going to Ukraine, we

00:00:39.157 --> 00:00:43.294
have Donald Trump to thank for

00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:44.062
that?
&gt;&gt; No.

00:00:44.062 --> 00:00:44.863
&gt;&gt; There's two militaries.

00:00:44.996 --> 00:00:45.764
&gt;&gt; There's two militaries?

00:00:45.897 --> 00:00:47.298
&gt;&gt; There's a good and a bad.

00:00:47.432 --> 00:00:48.933
&gt;&gt; So there's two militaries.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:49.734
Donald Trump is in charge of the

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:50.435
good one.

00:00:50.435 --> 00:00:52.537
&gt;&gt; Yes.
&gt;&gt; Biden's in charge of the bad

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:53.037
military?

00:00:53.037 --> 00:00:55.507
&gt;&gt; That's exactly right.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.674
&gt;&gt; All right.

00:00:56.808 --> 00:00:59.144
I've got my bottle of advil

00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:00.078
somewhere close by.

00:01:00.445 --> 00:01:01.780
This always happens, Jordan

00:01:01.913 --> 00:01:03.014
Klepper, when we have you on.

00:01:03.148 --> 00:01:04.449
My head starts to hurt.

00:01:04.449 --> 00:01:06.084
He joins us now.

00:01:06.451 --> 00:01:07.585
Jordan, two militaries?

00:01:07.719 --> 00:01:09.154
Where does this rank in terms of

00:01:09.287 --> 00:01:12.023
the more bizarre moments you've

00:01:12.457 --> 00:01:13.091
encountered at trump events?

00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:15.059
&gt;&gt; You know, it's up there

00:01:15.193 --> 00:01:16.461
although, you know, we've

00:01:16.461 --> 00:01:17.662
brought people back from the

00:01:17.796 --> 00:01:18.897
dead.
There's been body doubles out

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:19.731
there on the road.

00:01:19.864 --> 00:01:22.033
Two militaries, it's definitely

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:23.368
creative, but we haven't

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:27.338
summoned people back from death.

00:01:27.472 --> 00:01:28.473
So progress?

00:01:28.473 --> 00:01:29.007
&gt;&gt; Maybe so.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:30.475
And what was it like?

00:01:30.475 --> 00:01:32.477
I mean when you were there.

00:01:32.577 --> 00:01:33.945
You know, trump is talking about

00:01:34.078 --> 00:01:35.580
these smaller gatherings as if

00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:36.481
it's a plus.

00:01:36.481 --> 00:01:38.483
You know, we know trump and how

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:39.951
he likes large crowd sizes, and

00:01:40.084 --> 00:01:42.120
we don't need to go down that

00:01:42.487 --> 00:01:44.022
road.
But what is your sense of how

00:01:44.155 --> 00:01:46.090
his campaign is shaping up so

00:01:46.491 --> 00:01:47.759
&gt;&gt; Well, it was interesting.
far?

00:01:47.759 --> 00:01:50.495
You know, if you were expecting

00:01:50.495 --> 00:01:51.529
a spectacle, you weren't getting

00:01:51.663 --> 00:01:52.497
it there.

00:01:52.497 --> 00:01:53.465
It was confusing.

00:01:53.598 --> 00:01:54.499
There were people who came

00:01:54.632 --> 00:01:56.935
assuming it was a rally.

00:01:57.068 --> 00:01:59.938
Other folks called it a rally.

00:02:00.071 --> 00:02:02.507
Others called it an intimate

00:02:02.507 --> 00:02:07.011
event.
There were Maga people who were

00:02:07.145 --> 00:02:10.515
disappointed it wasn't a big

00:02:10.582 --> 00:02:11.983
event.
There's confusion in the air,

00:02:12.116 --> 00:02:14.519
which should be expected with a

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:16.521
trump campaign.

00:02:16.521 --> 00:02:19.023
I think overall, there's hope,

00:02:19.157 --> 00:02:20.525
at least interior-wise, that

00:02:20.525 --> 00:02:25.864
this is a new, better trump 3.0.

00:02:25.997 --> 00:02:27.098
Something that should be

00:02:27.232 --> 00:02:28.533
underlined with this event is

00:02:28.633 --> 00:02:30.001
these ideas were coming from

00:02:30.134 --> 00:02:32.537
people who went inside, who were

00:02:32.537 --> 00:02:34.539
invite-only.
So the folks that we ended up

00:02:34.539 --> 00:02:35.707
talking to out here, most of

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.775
them went inside, and they went

00:02:37.909 --> 00:02:38.676
inside because they're important

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:40.044
enough to have invitations to be

00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:42.547
in the front row of this GOP

00:02:42.614 --> 00:02:43.014
discussion.

00:02:43.014 --> 00:02:44.949
&gt;&gt; And I know you talked to

00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:45.917
another gentleman who appeared

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:47.418
to be at one point calling for

00:02:47.552 --> 00:02:50.688
an elevated discourse.

00:02:50.822 --> 00:02:52.190
I think we have some video.

00:02:52.557 --> 00:02:53.291
But his hat told another story.

00:02:53.424 --> 00:02:54.659
Can you tell us about that?

00:02:54.792 --> 00:02:56.561
&gt;&gt; Well, it's not uncommon to go

00:02:56.561 --> 00:02:57.929
to events where people talk

00:02:58.062 --> 00:03:00.565
about the things they want, and

00:03:00.565 --> 00:03:01.966
yet there's a hypocrisy that

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:03.868
they wear on their sleeve and/or

00:03:04.002 --> 00:03:04.502
cranium.

00:03:04.569 --> 00:03:05.303
And that was the situation here

00:03:05.436 --> 00:03:07.539
of somebody who arrived and

00:03:07.672 --> 00:03:08.640
talked about wanting to bring

00:03:08.773 --> 00:03:10.074
people together, that

00:03:10.208 --> 00:03:11.843
Republicans unlike Democrats

00:03:11.976 --> 00:03:13.711
come at this thing with a

00:03:13.845 --> 00:03:14.946
respectful dialogue and they

00:03:15.079 --> 00:03:16.214
respect the positions of power.

00:03:16.581 --> 00:03:17.749
And yet he was wearing a hat

00:03:17.882 --> 00:03:20.585
that said he could defecate a

00:03:20.618 --> 00:03:21.119
better president.

00:03:21.252 --> 00:03:22.720
We didn't challenge him on that,

00:03:22.854 --> 00:03:24.956
but we did challenge him on the

00:03:25.089 --> 00:03:26.624
inherent hypocrisy he brought to

00:03:26.758 --> 00:03:28.226
the rally slash intimate event.

00:03:28.593 --> 00:03:30.628
&gt;&gt; Yeah.
I have to ask you about it

00:03:30.762 --> 00:03:32.597
because I assume "The daily

00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:33.531
Show" will be covering it this

00:03:33.665 --> 00:03:34.999
week.
That is the biggest story of

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:36.601
this past week, the Chinese spy

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:38.136
balloon that was shot down after

00:03:38.269 --> 00:03:40.071
crossing the U.S.

00:03:40.204 --> 00:03:42.240
The balloon has also brought its

00:03:42.607 --> 00:03:43.107
share of mockery.

00:03:43.241 --> 00:03:43.775
Let's watch a little bit of

00:03:43.908 --> 00:03:46.978
"Snl" from last night.

00:03:47.111 --> 00:03:50.214
&gt;&gt; I entertain you people for

00:03:50.615 --> 00:03:53.518
four days and then get shot by

00:03:53.651 --> 00:03:53.952
Biden?

00:03:53.952 --> 00:03:56.721
I can't believe I'm Joe's Osama.

00:03:56.854 --> 00:03:57.989
&gt;&gt; I'm actually surprised you're

00:03:58.122 --> 00:03:58.957
still floating.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.825
Experts were saying you're the

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:02.627
size of three buses.

00:04:02.694 --> 00:04:03.027
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:04:03.027 --> 00:04:05.496
Ouch.

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:07.365
&gt;&gt; Jordan, I'm a little worried

00:04:07.498 --> 00:04:09.300
how you guys are going to be

00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:10.635
taking on the spy balloon this

00:04:10.768 --> 00:04:11.202
coming week.

00:04:11.202 --> 00:04:12.904
&gt;&gt; I think with respect, Jim.

00:04:13.037 --> 00:04:14.906
You know, a lot of people find

00:04:15.039 --> 00:04:15.707
humor in this.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.108
Other people could see an act of

00:04:17.241 --> 00:04:18.776
war.
You know, I've checked over on

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.212
Fox News, and I saw it purported

00:04:21.346 --> 00:04:22.313
to be an act of war.

00:04:22.647 --> 00:04:23.948
I also saw it mocked hours

00:04:24.082 --> 00:04:25.216
before, so it's confusing.

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:27.952
By I can guarantee you the daily

00:04:28.086 --> 00:04:29.187
Show" will take it with the

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.188
respect it deserves.

00:04:30.321 --> 00:04:31.823
&gt;&gt; I'm sure it will.

00:04:31.956 --> 00:04:34.325
Your colleague on the daily

00:04:34.659 --> 00:04:36.094
Show, Roy wood Jr., has been

00:04:36.227 --> 00:04:37.962
tapped to the entertainer at the

00:04:38.096 --> 00:04:38.730
white house correspondents'

00:04:38.863 --> 00:04:39.497
dinner this year.

00:04:39.631 --> 00:04:41.666
Any insights on what we can

00:04:41.799 --> 00:04:42.133
expect?

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.268
Will you be outside, you know,

00:04:44.669 --> 00:04:46.671
trying to get the pulse of the

00:04:46.804 --> 00:04:47.138
people?

00:04:47.138 --> 00:04:48.673
I'll try to slip past you

00:04:48.673 --> 00:04:51.442
unnoticed, but, you know --

00:04:51.576 --> 00:04:53.444
&gt;&gt; I would -- if Roy lets me be

00:04:53.578 --> 00:04:54.779
his plus-one, I will definitely

00:04:54.912 --> 00:04:55.947
be there.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.615
But there is a better chance

00:04:57.749 --> 00:04:58.883
that that goes to somebody else,

00:04:59.017 --> 00:05:00.718
and therefore I am outside.

00:05:00.852 --> 00:05:03.154
I will happily finger the pulse

00:05:03.287 --> 00:05:05.990
of anybody after his performance

00:05:06.124 --> 00:05:07.425
and try to get any kind of

00:05:07.558 --> 00:05:10.895
negative response that I can use

00:05:11.029 --> 00:05:12.764
against him as somebody who is

00:05:12.897 --> 00:05:13.665
oftentimes sharing an office

00:05:13.798 --> 00:05:14.298
with me.

00:05:14.365 --> 00:05:15.033
This one hurts.

00:05:15.166 --> 00:05:16.701
This is a big win for Roy.

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.102
He's going to be on the center

00:05:18.236 --> 00:05:18.703
stage.

00:05:18.703 --> 00:05:19.637
So whatever I can do to take him

00:05:19.771 --> 00:05:21.472
down a notch, I'll try it.

00:05:21.606 --> 00:05:24.075
&gt;&gt; And I'm sure he'll be taking

00:05:24.208 --> 00:05:25.309
us all down a notch, which is

00:05:25.443 --> 00:05:27.011
also a tradition of these

00:05:27.145 --> 00:05:27.478
dinners.

00:05:27.478 --> 00:05:29.681
As we're heading into the 2024

00:05:29.814 --> 00:05:30.948
campaign and that also makes my

00:05:31.082 --> 00:05:32.717
head hurt, thinking that we are

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:33.851
heading into the 2024 campaign

00:05:33.985 --> 00:05:35.520
this early on, I mean what do

00:05:35.653 --> 00:05:36.721
you think we're going to see?

00:05:36.821 --> 00:05:38.723
Are you going to get out there

00:05:38.756 --> 00:05:40.725
and see other campaign events

00:05:40.725 --> 00:05:41.225
besides trump?

00:05:43.961 --> 00:05:46.731
I mean what does your reporter's

00:05:46.731 --> 00:05:48.299
notebook look like in terms of

00:05:48.733 --> 00:05:49.333
the next steps?

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:50.735
What are you going to be out

00:05:50.768 --> 00:05:51.235
there covering?

00:05:51.235 --> 00:05:52.336
&gt;&gt; Well, we're excited to see

00:05:52.737 --> 00:05:55.373
how this all shapes up.

00:05:55.506 --> 00:05:56.874
Nikki Haley supposedly is having

00:05:57.008 --> 00:05:58.743
an event in the next week, and

00:05:58.743 --> 00:06:00.044
I'm very curious who shows up

00:06:00.178 --> 00:06:01.679
for that, what the dialogue

00:06:01.813 --> 00:06:02.747
around it is.

00:06:02.814 --> 00:06:05.616
On the GOP side, we're talking

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:06.350
to folks about what they think

00:06:06.751 --> 00:06:08.219
of Desantis.
Right now even at Maga events,

00:06:08.352 --> 00:06:10.154
Ron Desantis is not the bad guy.

00:06:10.288 --> 00:06:11.089
He's not seen as an alternative

00:06:11.222 --> 00:06:12.290
to trump.

00:06:12.423 --> 00:06:14.759
He's seen as a potential V.P.

00:06:14.892 --> 00:06:16.794
So I'm very curious to see if as

00:06:16.928 --> 00:06:18.996
the rhetoric gets hotter within

00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.499
the trump campaign, if those

00:06:21.632 --> 00:06:24.302
folks find defection, turn

00:06:24.435 --> 00:06:27.238
against somebody like Desantis.

00:06:27.371 --> 00:06:29.040
If Haley holds any sway.

00:06:29.173 --> 00:06:30.241
Who in the GOP is the voice of

00:06:30.374 --> 00:06:31.342
the people right now?

00:06:31.476 --> 00:06:33.411
I will say from this last rally,

00:06:33.544 --> 00:06:34.445
Lindsey graham was there, and I

00:06:34.779 --> 00:06:36.981
can tell you it's not Lindsey

00:06:37.115 --> 00:06:37.448
graham.

00:06:37.448 --> 00:06:39.383
&gt;&gt; Yes, I think you're right

00:06:39.517 --> 00:06:40.017
about that.

00:06:40.084 --> 00:06:41.886
But we know when you're going to

00:06:42.019 --> 00:06:43.221
be out there on the campaign

